{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1882092139825307941', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjoxNjAxNTc2ODc4MjIwOTAyNDAz', 'rest_id': '1601576878220902403', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': True, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Sat Dec 10 13:58:09 +0000 2022', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': "**This is my burner account** Wrestling fan, gamer, and Christian conservative. I'm blunt, but I don't bite 🤗", 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}, 'url': {'urls': [{'display_url': 'Bible.com', 'expanded_url': 'http://Bible.com', 'url': 'https://t.co/Z7l6GTCEKX', 'indices': [0, 23]}]}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 237525, 'followers_count': 1077, 'friends_count': 2945, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 9, 'location': 'United States', 'media_count': 6017, 'name': 'HTX Phantom🥋🐘🦬', 'normal_followers_count': 1077, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1857509631133888969'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1601576878220902403/1731084101', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1745269569281806336/c85HeMIB_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'HTXPhantom12', 'statuses_count': 39057, 'translator_type': 'none', 'url': 'https://t.co/Z7l6GTCEKX', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1882092139825307941'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1737564308000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '312', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/iphone" rel="nofollow">Twitter for iPhone</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4ODIwOTIxMzk1NzM1NTkyOTY=', 'text': 'From an 11 year Texas police officer’s opinion:\n\nI am not going to fully agree with everything he said for obvious reasons, such as why some states have completely outlawed red light cameras (because you could’ve been in the intersection legally but because traffic was so congested, you are still in it after the light turns red; people should not be cited because of that). \n\nWhat if someone were speeding because they were having a medical emergency? Or a complainant fleeing from a shooting? What if a vehicle was impeding traffic because of a sudden mechanical failure? AI monitoring traffic cameras would need to be able to make important distinctions, and I’m just not sure it would be able to do that for traffic monitoring. \n\nI also expect it to not be able to do that for other non-traffic, more serious offenses, because AI (in his example) would be limited to what it catches on video. What about what it ***doesn’t*** catch on video? This is why the human police officer can never be fully replaced.\n\nI couldn’t tell you how many times I’ve had to go to my neighbors porch to retrieve my own packages. That doesn’t mean I’m a porch pirate; instead, it means the delivery driver can’t read the numbers on the front of my house. Should an officer show up to handcuffs on me, based solely on the AI opinion of my neighbors surveillance video? Of course not.\n\nNow imagine sending a police officer out to respond to something easily explainable like that. Many departments don’t have the resources for that, especially within this defund the police movement. The system can’t handle a proactive system. It should stay reactive and people should only call when they feel there is a problem.\n\nI do like the idea of using drones and other advanced technologies for high-speed chases, because stuff like that protects officers from the reckless driving of eluding criminals.\n\nBut this man’s prescription for crime (including apparent unreported offenses) is a call for mass surveillance and it underestimates how many incidences occur within private residences—unless he is also calling for mass home surveillance as well. Should parents be arrested for spanking their children inside or outside the home?\n\nDANGEROUS TALK.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 22 15:45:08 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1882042989184430332', 'display_text_range': [14, 286], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 2, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd From an 11 year Texas police officer’s opinion:\n\nI am not going to fully agree with everything he said for obvious reasons, such as why some states have completely outlawed red light cameras (because you could’ve been in the intersection legally but because traffic was so', 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1882042989184430332', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 0, 'retweet_count': 0, 'retweeted': False, 'user_id_str': '1601576878220902403', 'id_str': '1882092139825307941'}}, '_legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 22 15:45:08 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1882042989184430332', 'display_text_range': [14, 286], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 2, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd From an 11 year Texas police officer’s opinion:\n\nI a